    "title": "Boil water advisory declared in Hammond - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Corbin Ross ,\n2 hours ago\nHAMMOND, La. ( WGNO ) — Tangipahoa Parish declared a limited precautionary boil water advisory for the Hammond area Wednesday, April 22.\nAccording to the Tangipahoa Water District, a contractor notified them of a leak on the six-inch main. Due to the loss of pressure during repair and out of an abundance of caution for the area, a boil water advisory was issued. It will remain in effect until it’s rescinded by the Water District.\nTangipahoa Parish deputies search for fisherman who reportedly drowned in Robert area The advisory applies to Happywoods Road from the corner of Adams Road south to West Hoffman Road, then east to the corner of Wagner Road and Adelle Road and the Bon Aire Subdivision.\nStay up to date with the latest news, weather and sports by downloading the WGNO app on the Apple or Google Play stores and by subscribing to the WGNO newsletter .\nLatest Posts Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WGNO.\n1",
